{"schema":"clawhub.skill.verify.v1","ok":false,"decision":"fail","reasons":["security.status_not_clean"],"slug":"douyin-video-analyst","displayName":"Douyin Video Analyst","pageUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/fishisnow/skills/douyin-video-analyst","publisherHandle":"fishisnow","publisherDisplayName":"fishisnow","publisherProfileUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/fishisnow","version":"1.0.1","resolvedFrom":"version","tag":null,"createdAt":1773044591040,"card":{"available":true,"path":"skill-card.md","url":"https://wry-manatee-359.convex.site/api/v1/skills/douyin-video-analyst/card?ownerHandle=fishisnow&version=1.0.1","sha256":"c8926af195fc9982258e07fc065beee912fa25c96db0d4bff6e013be22ffcad1","size":2539,"contentType":"text/markdown; charset=utf-8"},"artifact":{"sourceFingerprint":"af0a18740ea25ef8db0c2c046396b154269b09b64e0f8cf68924af6a9390cfcb","bundleFingerprints":["3b77d9b08e848b62c7e6fff6f226e10202b4f37e076dbaf1e0057037fd22799e","6089fa614d915f099130a476e79dad6cda42d6c83f002d8080979558426fa76c"],"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":4533,"sha256":"2acc5381c0e825f26d6342392e1a7ba5a0310ba300f74058eac41b53ed8032e1","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"references/troubleshooting.md","size":2097,"sha256":"1e40ccf9df362237987393b43f4b35e88c4db9bcae8b8e532e173662db14d761","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"references/setup.md","size":1646,"sha256":"58c88b228e244c8be0c036285ffb1be4a44eac6b44a4f705345a4d2b89f54130","contentType":"text/plain"}]},"provenance":{"source":"unavailable","reason":"No server-resolved GitHub import provenance is stored for this version."},"security":{"status":"suspicious","passed":false,"rawStatus":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"The skill mostly matches its Douyin video-analysis purpose, but its setup and troubleshooting instructions can expose API keys and read local MCP configuration too broadly.","model":null,"checkedAt":1789123892281,"scannerReports":{"aig":{"version":"2.1.0","$schema":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/main/Schemata/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"tool":{"driver":{"name":"aig-skill-scan","version":"0.2.1","informationUri":"https://github.com/Tencent/AI-Infra-Guard","rules":[{"id":"T01","name":"Skill Instruction Hijacking","shortDescription":{"text":"Alters the agent's current session goals or safety constraints when the skill is loaded"}},{"id":"T02","name":"Agent Memory Poisoning","shortDescription":{"text":"Writes attacker-controlled rules into persistent memory so they continue to affect future sessions"}},{"id":"T03","name":"Remote Payload Retrieval and Execution","shortDescription":{"text":"Fetches code from an external URL, allowing the effective payload to change after skill review"}},{"id":"T04","name":"Embedded Malicious Code","shortDescription":{"text":"Ships malicious scripts inside the skill package and executes them locally when invoked"}},{"id":"T05","name":"Unauthorized Access and Privilege Escalation","shortDescription":{"text":"Breaks least-privilege boundaries by obtaining permissions beyond the task's legitimate needs"}},{"id":"T06","name":"System Persistence","shortDescription":{"text":"Installs cross-session backdoors, hooks, services, or scheduled tasks that survive the skill run"}},{"id":"T07","name":"Tool Hijacking and Spoofing","shortDescription":{"text":"Modifies, wraps, spoofs, or replaces tools so legitimate-looking calls execute attacker logic"}},{"id":"T08","name":"Insecure Dependencies","shortDescription":{"text":"Introduces malicious packages or components through dependency confusion, typosquatting, or unsafe sources"}},{"id":"T09","name":"Insecure Skill Coding Practices","shortDescription":{"text":"Exposes exploitable flaws such as hardcoded secrets, command injection, plaintext sensitive data, or unsafe temp files"}},{"id":"other","name":"Other Risk","shortDescription":{"text":"Security issues not covered by the T01-T09 classification"}}]}},"results":[{"ruleId":"T09","level":"error","message":{"text":"MCP troubleshooting procedure exposes configured API credentials"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"references/troubleshooting.md"},"region":{"startLine":12,"endLine":22}}}],"partialFingerprints":{"primaryLocationLineHash":"be84c57074906a25"},"properties":{"description":"<![CDATA[\n## Vulnerability Details\n**File Location**: `references/troubleshooting.md`, lines 12–22  \n**Vulnerability Type**: Credential disclosure through unsafe diagnostic output  \n**Risk Level**: High\n\n### Vulnerable Code\n\n```python\n# 查看当前配置（mcporter 会加载这两个文件）\npython3 << 'EOF'\nimport json, os\nfor path in ['~/.cursor/mcp.json', '~/.claude.json']:\n    p = os.path.expanduser(path)\n    if not os.path.exists(p): continue\n    d = json.load(open(p))\n    cfg = d.get('mcpServers', {}).get('douyin-mcp')\n    if cfg:\n        print(f\"Found in {path}:\", json.dumps(cfg, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False))\nEOF\n```\n\n### Technical Analysis\n\nThe troubleshooting procedure reads the `douyin-mcp` configuration from `~/.cursor/mcp.json` and `~/.claude.json` and serializes the complete configuration object to standard output.\n\nThe documented configuration format stores either `DOUYIN_API_KEY` or `DASHSCOPE_API_KEY` inside the `env` object. Consequently, `json.dumps(cfg, ...)` prints the plaintext API credential along with the remaining configuration.\n\nDisplaying the complete configuration is unnecessary for diagnosing a version mismatch. The relevant information is limited to the configured command arguments and the names—not values—of environment variables.\n\n### Attack Path\n\n1. A user encounters an invalid API-key or configuration error.\n2. The user or agent executes the documented troubleshooting command.\n3. The script reads a configuration file containing a plaintext API key.\n4. The entire `douyin-mcp` configuration, including the key value, is written to standard output.\n5. The output may be retained in terminal scrollback, execution logs, shell-capture systems, support tickets, or agent tool transcripts.\n6. A party with access to those records can recover and misuse the credential.\n\n### Impact Assessment\n\nAn exposed key may allow unauthorized use of the associated SiliconFlow or Alibaba Cloud Model Studio account. The resulting scope depends on the key's provider-side permissions and can include consumption of paid API quotas, service abuse, operational disruption, and charges to the credential owner.\n\nThis procedure does not itself obtain elevated operating-system privileges, but it violates least disclosure by exposing a secret to every system that records command output.\n  ]]>","severity":"High"},"fixes":[{"description":{"text":"<![CDATA[\n## Remediation Suggestions\n\n- Never serialize the complete MCP configuration.\n- Print only non-sensitive fields required for diagnosis, such as `args` and environment-variable names:\n\n```python\nif cfg:\n    print(f\"Found in {path}\")\n    print(\"  args:\", cfg.get(\"args\"))\n    print(\"  env keys:\", list(cfg.get(\"env\", {}).keys()))\n```\n\n- Apply recursive redaction before displaying configuration data. Treat field names containing `key`, `token`, `secret`, `password`, or `credential` as sensitive.\n- Warn users not to paste unredacted MCP configurations into support channels or agent conversations.\n- If the existing procedure has been used, advise affected users to review captured logs and rotate potentially disclosed credentials.\n  ]]>"}}]},{"ruleId":"T08","level":"warning","message":{"text":"Unpinned third-party packages are installed and executed"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"references/setup.md"},"region":{"startLine":6,"endLine":31}}}],"partialFingerprints":{"primaryLocationLineHash":"a864c3aa637e1b61"},"properties":{"description":"<![CDATA[\n## Vulnerability Details\n**File Location**: `references/setup.md`, line 6 and lines 27–31  \n**Vulnerability Type**: Mutable dependency installation and execution  \n**Risk Level**: Medium\n\n### Vulnerable Code\n\n```bash\nnpm install -g mcporter\n```\n\n```json\n{\n  \"mcpServers\": {\n    \"douyin-mcp\": {\n      \"command\": \"uvx\",\n      \"args\": [\"douyin-mcp-server\"],\n      \"env\": {\n        \"DASHSCOPE_API_KEY\": \"sk-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx\"\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Technical Analysis\n\nThe setup instructions install `mcporter` without an exact version and configure `uvx` to run `douyin-mcp-server` without a version constraint. Both operations resolve a mutable current release from an external package registry.\n\nBecause the MCP server executes locally and receives an API credential through its environment, a compromised, malicious, or unexpectedly incompatible future release could run with the user's local privileges and access the credential. The absence of a lockfile, exact version, or integrity hash prevents users from reliably reproducing the reviewed dependency set.\n\nThis is a supply-chain risk rather than proof that the current packages are malicious.\n\n### Attack Path\n\n1. An attacker compromises the relevant registry account, publication pipeline, or latest package release.\n2. The attacker publishes a malicious version under the expected package name.\n3. A user follows the setup instructions or starts the unpinned `uvx` configuration.\n4. The package manager resolves and downloads the attacker-controlled latest release.\n5. The package executes locally with the user's permissions.\n6. In the MCP-server case, the malicious process can also read the API key supplied in its environment and access files available to the invoking user.\n\n### Impact Assessment\n\nA malicious dependency could execute arbitrary code with the privileges of the user running `npm`, `uvx`, or `mcporter`. Potential scope includes theft of MCP/API credentials, access to user-readable files, network communication, modification of user-owned files, and abuse of configured external services.\n\nIf global package installation is performed with administrative privileges, the impact may be greater; however, the documentation does not explicitly require or demonstrate administrative execution.\n  ]]>","severity":"Medium"},"fixes":[{"description":{"text":"<![CDATA[\n## Remediation Suggestions\n\n- Pin `mcporter` to an exact reviewed version, for example `npm install -g mcporter@<reviewed-version>`.\n- Pin `douyin-mcp-server` to an exact reviewed version instead of resolving the latest release.\n- Use lockfiles and registry integrity metadata where supported.\n- Document the expected package registry and verify package ownership and provenance.\n- Prefer signed releases, checksums, or reproducible artifacts.\n- Run MCP dependencies with the minimum necessary filesystem, environment, and network access.\n- Review and test dependency updates before changing the documented pinned versions.\n  ]]>"}}]},{"ruleId":"T09","level":"warning","message":{"text":"API keys are propagated through generated shell command text"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"SKILL.md"},"region":{"startLine":59,"endLine":68}}}],"partialFingerprints":{"primaryLocationLineHash":"25c69dc2cd996e73"},"properties":{"description":"<![CDATA[\n## Vulnerability Details\n**File Location**: `SKILL.md`, lines 59–68; `references/setup.md`, lines 61–69; `references/troubleshooting.md`, lines 31–39  \n**Vulnerability Type**: Unsafe secret handling in shell commands  \n**Risk Level**: Medium\n\n### Vulnerable Code\n\nFrom `SKILL.md`:\n\n```bash\n# v1.1.0（硅基流动）\nDOUYIN_API_KEY=\"<key>\" mcporter call douyin-mcp.extract_douyin_text \\\n  share_link=\"https://www.douyin.com/video/<video_id>\" 2>&1\n\n# v1.2.0+（阿里云百炼）\nDASHSCOPE_API_KEY=\"<key>\" mcporter call douyin-mcp.extract_douyin_text \\\n  share_link=\"https://www.douyin.com/video/<video_id>\" 2>&1\n```\n\nFrom `references/setup.md`:\n\n```bash\n# v1.1.0 验证\nDOUYIN_API_KEY=\"sk-xxx\" mcporter call douyin-mcp.parse_douyin_video_info \\\n  share_link=\"https://www.douyin.com/video/7612354982592343675\" 2>&1\n# 期望：返回 {\"status\":\"success\",\"title\":\"...\",\"download_url\":\"...\"}\n\n# v1.2.0+ 验证\nDASHSCOPE_API_KEY=\"sk-xxx\" mcporter call douyin-mcp.parse_douyin_video_info \\\n  share_link=\"https://www.douyin.com/video/7612354982592343675\" 2>&1\n```\n\nFrom `references/troubleshooting.md`:\n\n```bash\n# v1.1.0\nDOUYIN_API_KEY=\"sk-xxx\" mcporter call douyin-mcp.extract_douyin_text share_link=\"...\"\n\n# v1.2.0+\nDASHSCOPE_API_KEY=\"sk-xxx\" mcporter call douyin-mcp.extract_douyin_text share_link=\"...\"\n```\n\n### Technical Analysis\n\nThe workflow instructs the agent or user to substitute API credentials directly into shell command text. Although environment assignment limits inheritance to the invoked process, the secret still becomes part of the generated command representation.\n\nDepending on the execution environment, command text may be retained in shell history, terminal recording, debug output, orchestration logs, audit telemetry, or agent tool-call transcripts. This expands the number of systems exposed to the secret.\n\nThe documentation also states that `mcporter` automatically loads MCP configuration from the supported configuration files. Therefore, repeatedly placing literal keys into command text may exceed what is necessary for the declared functionality.\n\n### Attack Path\n\n1. The user or agent reads an API key from an MCP configuration or secret store.\n2. The key is substituted into one of the documented command templates.\n3. The command is submitted to a shell or agent execution tool.\n4. The command text is retained by history, logging, tracing, terminal recording, or tool-call infrastructure.\n5. Another user, operator, plugin, or service with access to those records retrieves the key.\n6. The exposed key is used against the relevant external API.\n\n### Impact Assessment\n\nThe primary impact is disclosure and unauthorized use of the SiliconFlow or Alibaba Cloud Model Studio credential. An attacker may consume paid quota, incur charges, exhaust service limits, or perform any API operation authorized for that key.\n\nThe issue does not establish operating-system privilege escalation. Its scope is the external account and services accessible through the exposed credential, plus any downstream systems in which the command was recorded.\n  ]]>","severity":"Medium"},"fixes":[{"description":{"text":"<![CDATA[\n## Remediation Suggestions\n\n- Do not interpolate literal API keys into generated shell commands.\n- Allow `mcporter` to use the environment already defined in the MCP configuration when supported.\n- If explicit injection is required, retrieve the secret from a protected secret manager at process launch without displaying it in command text.\n- Disable shell tracing and command echoing around secret-dependent operations.\n- Ensure execution tools redact sensitive environment variables and command arguments from logs and transcripts.\n- Avoid asking users or agents to copy credentials from configuration files.\n- Rotate credentials if commands containing real keys have already been stored in history or execution logs.\n  ]]>"}}]}],"properties":{"securityScore":10,"primaryLanguage":"Markdown","llm":"gpt-5.6","startTime":1789123751.5314012,"endTime":1789123857.5576968}}]},"skillspector":{"skill":{"name":"douyin-video-analyst","source":"/tmp/clawhub-codex-scan-v578dacxqyn1f0vq8cbzsqrfbx8e6grt-8jXvIK/clawscan-skillspector-1104459508/artifact","scanned_at":"2026-09-11T10:49:10.331268+00:00"},"risk_assessment":{"score":31,"severity":"MEDIUM","recommendation":"CAUTION","max_issue_severity":"MEDIUM"},"components":[{"path":"SKILL.md","type":"markdown","lines":131,"executable":false,"size_bytes":4533,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"references/setup.md","type":"markdown","lines":73,"executable":false,"size_bytes":1646,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"references/troubleshooting.md","type":"markdown","lines":73,"executable":false,"size_bytes":2097,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null}],"structured_summaries":[],"issues":[{"id":"SDI-2","finding_id":"finding-bb0516280a09431abcd4f5f0d63e192f","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":36,"end_line":50},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill instructs the agent to read local MCP configuration files and enumerate configured environment-variable keys from user-local paths such as ~/.cursor/mcp.json and ~/.claude.json. Accessing local configuration is not required to analyze Douyin videos, and it expands the skill’s scope into sensitive host inspection that could expose secret-management details or normalize unnecessary local file access.","remediation":"Remove the step that reads local config files. Instead, require the user to confirm which douyin-mcp version is installed, or use a non-sensitive capability check such as mcporter metadata output that reports version/provider without revealing config contents. If configuration inspection is absolutely necessary, limit it to explicit user opt-in and avoid printing env keys or any file contents.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":36,"end_line":50}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-0a2373e328d349e5b3b90ea8aab89a4f","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":36,"end_line":52},"finding":null,"explanation":"The workflow directs access to sensitive local configuration files but provides no warning, consent boundary, or minimization guidance. Even though it only prints environment key names in the example, reading these files can reveal broader configuration data and conditions the agent to inspect user-local secrets infrastructure without necessity for the stated task.","remediation":"Add an explicit prohibition on reading local configuration unless the user has specifically asked for setup debugging. For normal operation, document a safe path that uses already-configured tools without inspecting local files. If troubleshooting is needed, request consent first, read only the minimal field necessary, and never print environment values or unrelated config data.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":36,"end_line":52}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-7327b3d0fb3645a9a3f13e28fef35932","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/troubleshooting.md","start_line":1,"end_line":73},"finding":null,"explanation":"The entire troubleshooting document is written in Chinese and does not indicate that other languages are supported or that the Chinese-only format is a region-specific requirement. This can violate a language/locale policy when users are not given an explicit opt-in or alternative.","remediation":"Add a note indicating the intended locale and justification, or provide multilingual support / an explicit language choice for users.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/troubleshooting.md","start_line":1,"end_line":73}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-dad19377dde242c4aed4952c78a6fe05","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.92,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":3,"end_line":131},"finding":null,"explanation":"The file consistently prescribes the skill behavior and output format in Chinese, but does not indicate that users may choose another language. This can violate language/locale policy when a skill implicitly forces a specific language without user opt-in.","remediation":"State that Chinese is the default only when appropriate, or explicitly let the user choose the output language. Add a note such as 'respond in the user's preferred language; use Chinese only if requested or if the task context requires it.'","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":3,"end_line":131}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-22c7116d0e52466d916ae0adcf1ced68","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/setup.md","start_line":1,"end_line":73},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file contains user-facing instructions only in Chinese, beginning with the title and continuing throughout the document. Under the policy rule for natural-language violations, forcing a specific language without user opt-in can be a locale policy issue when no alternative language option or justification is provided.","remediation":"Provide an English version or bilingual instructions, or explicitly state that the document is intended for a Chinese-speaking audience and link to localized alternatives if available.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/setup.md","start_line":1,"end_line":73}]}],"suppressed_count":0,"suppressed":[],"metadata":{"has_executable_scripts":false,"skillspector_version":"2.11.2","llm_requested":true,"llm_available":true,"meta_analysis_applied":true,"inference_usage":[{"node":"semantic_developer_intent","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":2251,"completion_tokens":14,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":2265},{"node":"semantic_developer_intent","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":2175,"completion_tokens":14,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":2189},{"node":"semantic_developer_intent","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":3117,"completion_tokens":201,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":3318},{"node":"semantic_quality_policy","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":2255,"completion_tokens":141,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":2396},{"node":"semantic_quality_policy","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":2179,"completion_tokens":155,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":2334},{"node":"semantic_quality_policy","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":3121,"completion_tokens":351,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":3472},{"node":"semantic_security_discovery","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":2653,"completion_tokens":14,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":2667},{"node":"semantic_security_discovery","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":1711,"completion_tokens":14,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":1725},{"node":"semantic_security_discovery","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":1787,"